<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kangshu Feng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Kang Shu Feng, Kangshu of Wey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kangshu Feng was a younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wu-of-zhou">King Wu of Zhou</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rebellion-of-the-three-guards">Rebellion of the Three Guards</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a> granted him the former Shang capital region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhaoge">Zhaoge</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> to watch over the conquered Shang population. He founded the state of Wey, which survived as the last Zhou state until 209 BCE.</p></div>
